From 029ef4cf0755f5e82d901d733ae187fc9580f981 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:27:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Preserve lexical keyword identity in exec descriptor
 carry

Why: quote removal turned ordinary fi/done/} commands into scope closers.
A conditional close then incorrectly discarded the parent descriptor's
reachable script. Preserve quoted/escaped provenance on ShellWord and
stop reserved-word peeling at literal commands. Remove the redundant
quote-unaware peel that could reinterpret a quoted opener's exec argument.

Proof: review-head closer regressions fail 6 cases; the initial repair
fails four quoted opener cases. Fixed tests exercise harmless real Bash
markers for quoted closers/openers and pipeline/background closes.
Full cron before the last three added pipeline tests: 10971 passed,
0 failed, 9 skipped; latest focused carry/keyword set 114 passed.
External lifecycle consumers: 380 passed. Eleven targeted safety mutants
killed; pipeline successor mutant initially survived and was killed by
three added real-Bash controls.

Nonblocking scope-restoration overblocking belongs to t_b24e8be58433ed41;
implicit stdin/variable descriptors/eval to t_85a717e32585c741.
Final-head real-row replay and independent review/CI remain landing gates.
